WEBVTT

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.640
Your users open the app and wait
for a list they loaded a minute ago.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.720
Then the signal drops in the middle of a
form and everything they typed is gone.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.740
WaveMaker fixes both with one
idea, the API Interceptor.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.000
It sits between a service variable and the
network and decides what happens to every call.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.120
Forget calls, turn on

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.120
caching, and repeat requests
are answered from the device.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.400
The first call goes to
the server and is stored.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.460
The next ones come straight
from the cache until it expires.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.480
Choose where it lives.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.120
A session cache is fast and
clears when the app closes.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.640
A persistent cache survives restarts, so
the data is there even when the app opens

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:07.560
offline. Turn on Refresh in
background, and users see cached

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.040
data instantly, while a fresh
call quietly updates it.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.720
By default, cached data stays valid for
five minutes, and the cache keeps up to a

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:22.140
hundred entries, removing expired ones
first, then the least recently used.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:30.220
For post, put, and delete, you
write the intercept script yourself.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:37.460
When the device is online, call context.proceed
and the request goes out as usual.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:44.680
When it's offline, save the request on the
device and return a value so the screen

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:50.640
keeps working. When the connection
comes back, network service on network

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.620
change tells your app and
you send what was saved.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:03.550
Open settings, app configurations, API
interceptors, and add an interceptor for any

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:04.570
service you've imported.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:11.940
The dashboard lists them all, and you can filter
by method or by type, cache or custom.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:20.000
Prefer one switch? Turn on caching
for the whole app in wm_rn_config.json

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.010
and every get is cached.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:28.050
And leave specific services out by
listing their URLs under exclude.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:32.720
Fast when you're connected,
safe when you're not.
